      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The development of two-dimensional conformal field theory made exact solutions possible for a broad class of critical phenomena and became a foundational framework across statistical physics and field theory.",
        "attribution": "Belavin, Polyakov, and Zamolodchikov jointly established the central framework and its exact methods; credit among the three is well aligned with the discovery described.",
        "maturity": "The theory has had decades of extensive use and confirmation in critical systems.",
        "uncertainties": [
