      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit quantum electrodynamics established a practical and conceptually clear way to couple superconducting artificial atoms to microwave photons, enabling major advances in quantum control.",
        "attribution": "Blais supplied key theoretical architecture, while Wallraff and Schoelkopf led pivotal experimental demonstrations; together they represent complementary contributions.",
        "maturity": "The platform has been replicated, refined, and used extensively, though its ultimate role in scalable quantum computation is still developing.",
